# Data 360 dual-report & chat starters

## When the user starts a chat or asks what to run

Offer **suggestion prompts** from [prompts/chat-starters.md](../../prompts/chat-starters.md)
(and the copy-paste block in [prompts/example-prompts.md](../../prompts/example-prompts.md)).
Prefer prompts that already name **dataspace + populated DMO(s)** so you do not re-ask
routing questions.

Recommended first offers (one HCP Stage + one DTC):

1. STG-US HQ email opens 90d on `stg_Headquarter_Email_Engagement__dlm`
2. DTC Premarin brand + opt-in on `DTC_BrandProfile__dlm` + `DTC_ContactPointConsent__dlm`

## Every count answer (HCP and DTC)

1. **Query Data 360 only** for the live count. Do **not** check Snowflake MCP connectivity,
   call `mcp_auth` on Snowflake, or probe the Snowflake connector.
2. Dual-report **table**: Data 360 row (live count) + Snowflake source row marked **PENDING**
   (or **N/A** if the stream is not Snowflake-fed) + Delta **PENDING** / **N/A**.
3. Always include the exact **Snowflake validation SQL** under the table (same filters / person
   grain as the D360 count).
4. Always include this note:

> **Note:** Snowflake is not queried via MCP. Run the validation SQL in Snowflake to complete the dual report; the Data 360 count above is live from Data 360.

5. Always include **links** under the table:
   - **Data 360 DMO link** for each primary fact DMO in the count — resolve `id` with
     `d360_dmo_get`, then
     `https://pfizer-cdp-us--cfcstage.sandbox.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/MktDataModelObject/<dmoId>/view`
     (swap host if the org context differs).
   - **Data 360 segment link** when the ask is a segment create/update/status **or** a matching
     MarketSegment exists:
     `https://pfizer-cdp-us--cfcstage.sandbox.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/MarketSegment/<marketSegmentId>/view`.
     For pure DMO/SQL counts with no MarketSegment, write
     `Data 360 segment link: N/A — DMO count only (no MarketSegment)`.
6. Do not invent empty-path demos (Stage profiles/consent; Dev geo/consent; DTC email engagement audiences).
